---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';
import checks from '../../../../../public/equipment/08-02/verification.json';
import m from '../../../../../public/equipment/08-02/interactions.json';
const a='/equipment/08-02/',op='https://apachepersonal.miun.se/~gorthu/K%26S%204524/94500-000D-000-01.pdf',kth='https://www.nanophys.kth.se/nanolab/bonder/bonder.html',mmf='https://mmf.montana.edu/documents/equipment-operating-manuals/KS%20452A%20Wire%20Bonder%20Manual-Accessible.pdf';
const fields=[['spanUm','Pad span X (µm)',250,2000,500],['apexUm','Loop centerline apex (µm)',30,400,120],['widthUm','Ribbon width (µm)',25,200,127],['thicknessUm','Thickness (µm)',5,50,25],['blockXUm','Obstacle center X (µm)',0,2000,250],['blockLengthUm','Obstacle length X (µm)',10,400,100],['blockOffsetUm','Obstacle lateral offset Y (µm)',-400,400,0],['blockWidthUm','Obstacle width Y (µm)',10,400,100],['blockHeightUm','Obstacle top Z (µm)',0,400,115],['marginUm','Required gap (µm)',0,100,15],['orientationDeg','Foot direction (°)',-180,180,0]];
const show=x=>typeof x==='string'?x:Object.entries(x).map(([k,v])=>k+': '+(typeof v==='number'?Number(v.toPrecision(8)):String(v))).join('; ');
---
<Layout pageTitle="K&S 4523D ribbon layout bench" subtitle="" description="Inspect a wedge bonder and check inert ribbon clearance between package pads." wide={true}>
<article id="bond" class="equipment"><nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/08-02/">← Equipment 08-02</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Equipment register</a><a href="#bond-proof">Verification</a></nav>
<header><p class="eq-meta">08-02 / Assembly geometry / Virtual wedge-bonder bench</p><h2>Kulicke &amp; Soffa 4523D</h2><p>Check an inert ribbon route over a package obstacle. The 120 µm apex collides; switch to the 160 µm reference and evaluate again to get 26.1 µm of vertical clearance.</p></header>
<div class="e-grid"><section class="e-card"><h3>01 · Inspect the bonder</h3><div id="bond-views" class="e-row">{['Bench','Front','Side','Work'].map(k=><button data-view={k.toLowerCase()}>{k}</button>)}<button id="bond-xr" disabled>VR unavailable</button></div>
<canvas id="bond-model" aria-label="Orbitable manual K and S wedge bonder"></canvas><p id="bond-asset" role="status">Loading metric GLB…</p><p>Drag to orbit; scroll or pinch to zoom. Click the holder to seat/lift, the lever to change the virtual loop preset, or the keypad to check the design. These mappings are teaching interactions, not physical bonder controls.</p></section>
<section class="e-card"><h3>02 · Configure the geometry</h3><form id="bond-form"><div class="e-row"><button id="bond-seat" type="button">Lift package</button><button id="bond-apex" type="button">Toggle 120/160 µm apex</button></div><div class="e-fields"><label>Specimen ID<input name="sampleId" value="package-fanout-01" required maxlength="96"/></label>{fields.map(([k,t,l,h,v])=><label>{t}<input name={k} type="number" min={l} max={h} step="any" value={v}/></label>)}</div>
<div class="e-row"><button id="bond-run" type="submit" class="e-run">Evaluate ribbon</button><button id="bond-reset" type="button">Restore example</button></div></form><p id="bond-status" role="status">Package seated.</p></section></div>
<section class="e-card"><h3>03 · Inspect the clearance</h3><p id="bond-result" role="status">No clearance checked.</p><svg id="bond-chart" viewBox="0 0 550 200" role="img" aria-label="Side profile of the ribbon envelope and inert keep-out block"></svg><p>Package-local section; the obstacle is faded when it does not overlap the ribbon laterally. The macro GLB shows the workholding, not microscopic contacts.</p><div class="e-row"><button id="bond-json" disabled>Assembly JSON</button><button id="bond-csv" disabled>Ribbon points CSV</button></div></section>
<section><h3>Selected machine and references</h3><p>Digital 4523D in a vertical-feed accessory family. The <a href={op}>K&amp;S P/N 94500-000D-000-01 Rev 03/02</a> lists 680 × 530 × 700 mm W/H/D (p. 1-6), a 0.750-inch wedge option (pp. 5-1–2), and a 1 × 5 mil ribbon entry in Table 5-1. The teaching cross-section (25 × 127 µm) is a rounded geometry input, not an instruction to configure a real tool. Compare <a href={kth}>KTH 4523D image</a> and <a href={mmf}>Montana MMF 4523AD, figs. 1–2</a> for operator/workholder detail. Small fixtures, ports, shell transitions and motion are inferred.</p>
<div class="e-grid"><figure><img src={a+'front.svg'} width="760" height="450" alt="Original metric K and S wedge bonder projection"/></figure><figure><img src={a+'work.svg'} width="760" height="450" alt="Original workholder and wedge geometry"/></figure></div></section>
<section><h3>Geometry and export contract</h3><p>From pad A to B, z(x) = max(t/2, 4H(x/L)(1−x/L)). A rectangular ribbon uses this centerline and a vertical thickness t. If its width overlaps the obstacle laterally, minimum lower-edge clearance across the obstacle occurs at one end of its X overlap. Any nonpositive gap is a collision; a positive gap below the requested margin still fails. A rotated rectangular bond footprint must fit each virtual 200 × 180 µm pad. Coordinates: X pad A to B, Y across substrate, Z up.</p>
<p>Input geometry is a package ID, pad span, cross-section, apex, keep-out and footprint orientation. Export preserves PAD-A/PAD-B, revisions, footprints, sampled envelope, min gap and provenance. Ideal connectivity is only geometry eligibility, not measured electrical continuity, strength, ultrasonic bonding, material damage or release criteria. <a href={a+'output-schema.json'}>Schema</a> · <a href={a+'example-result.json'}>Example</a>.</p></section>
<section id="bond-proof"><h3>Verification and files</h3><div class="e-over"><table><thead><tr><th>Case</th><th>Expected</th><th>Actual</th><th>Status</th></tr></thead><tbody>{checks.map(r=><tr><td>{r.id}</td><td>{show(r.expected)}</td><td>{show(r.actual)}</td><td>{r.pass?'Pass':'Fail'}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
<p><a href={a+'reference-plan.json'}>Predeclared checks</a> · <a href={a+'verification.json'}>Verification JSON</a> · <a href={a+'ks-4523d.glb'} download>GLB</a> · <a href={a+'geometry-source.mjs'}>Editable geometry</a> + <a href={a+'make-model.mjs'}>build script</a> + <a href={a+'mesh-writer.mjs'}>mesh writer</a> · <a href={a+'interactions.json'}>WebXR anchors</a>. {m.triangles.toLocaleString()} triangles, {m.draws} draw primitives. Physical headset untested.</p></section></article></Layout>
<script>import '../../../../lib/equipment/08-02/client.mjs';</script>
<style>
#bond header{max-width:73ch;padding:1.3rem 0}#bond h2{font-size:clamp(2rem,6vw,4rem);margin:.2rem 0}#bond section{margin:1rem 0}.e-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1rem}.e-card{border:1px solid var(--border);padding:.8rem;min-width:0}.e-card h3{margin:.3rem 0}.e-row{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.4rem;margin:.5rem 0}.e-fields{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.55rem}.e-fields label{display:grid;gap:.2rem}.e-fields input,#bond button{min-width:0;min-height:2.45rem;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:3px;background:var(--panel);color:var(--text);font:inherit;padding:.3rem .5rem;box-sizing:border-box}#bond button:disabled{opacity:.52}.e-run{background:#3d596e!important;color:white!important}#bond-model{width:100%;height:clamp(280px,34vw,440px);display:block;background:#ebe8e0;touch-action:none}#bond-chart{width:100%;max-height:13rem}.e-over{overflow:auto}#bond table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:.85rem}#bond td,#bond th{text-align:left;padding:.45rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)}#bond figure{margin:0}#bond img{width:100%;height:auto}@media(max-width:820px){.e-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.e-fields{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))}}
</style>
